from research_helpers import source, assessment, record, scope, evidence, decision, write_batch

refs=[
 ('remnant','Remnant','Mass Effect: Andromeda Wiki contributors','https://masseffectandromeda.fandom.com/wiki/Remnant','Jardaan infrastructure terraforms worlds and seeded angaran life, before the Scourge disrupted it.','Origins and environmental engineering do not establish ordinary angaran household allocation.'),
 ('forerunner','Forerunner','Halopedia contributors','https://www.halopedia.org/Forerunner','Bounded society/technology sections describe occupational rates, council authority and advanced ancillas.','Hierarchy, ceremonial ship commands and powerful technology do not establish ordinary work-independent food/housing entitlements; no novels were read.'),
 ('created','Created','Halopedia contributors','https://www.halopedia.org/Created','Cortana promises to address hunger, poverty and illness after peace while deploying coercive Guardians.','A promised welfare future is distinct from an implemented universal provision system.'),
 ('ancestors','Ancestors','Halopedia contributors','https://www.halopedia.org/Ancestors','Ancient humans field advanced technology, then suffer defeat, devolution and preservation experiments.','Military parity and stored patterns are not an ordinary prewar resource-access constitution.'),
 ('ueg','Unified Earth Government','Halopedia contributors','https://www.halopedia.org/United_Earth_Government','Civilian government and UNSC emergency rule vary across periods and colonies.','Institutional government alone does not prove household automatic provision. Forum suggestions that the military is a jobs program were discarded.'),
 ('covenant','Covenant technical personnel','Halopedia contributors','https://www.halopedia.org/Covenant_Loyalists','Huragok perform technological maintenance, excavation and medical work.','A specific faction/species-role reference does not establish all original Covenant civilian distribution; artificial biological workers are still useful persons.'),
 ('golden-age','Golden Age','Destinypedia contributors','https://www.destinypedia.com/Golden_Age','Traveler-enabled technologies accompany corporations, research, colonization and Exo creation.','No general automatic necessities allocation is established by the short history; a forum’s post-scarcity label was not treated as proof.'),
 ('last-city','Last City','Destinypedia contributors','https://www.destinypedia.com/City','Civilian science, supply crises, quarantine work and defense continue in the protected city.','Safety under the Traveler is not a verified complete household material floor; role-playing economies were discarded.'),
 ('vex','Vex','Destinypedia contributors','https://www.destinypedia.com/Vex','Cyber-organic life works continuously to convert worlds into machinery.','A converting collective and captured minds are not automatically a supported human post-work population.'),
 ('exo','Beyond Light collector’s journal analysis','GameSpot staff (individual byline not checked)','https://www.gamespot.com/articles/destiny-2-beyond-light-collectors-edition-and-arg-illuminate-the-stranger-deep-stone-crypt/1100-6484379/','Clovis Bray experiments on human subjects, develops Exo bodies and uses memory wipes to maintain them.','The article summarizes released collector material; no ARG decoding, complete journal reading or assumption of a leisure society was undertaken.'),
 ('orokin','Orokin','WARFRAME Wiki contributors','https://warframe.fandom.com/wiki/Orokin','The reference explicitly describes selective rejection of robotic automation/true machine intelligence despite technical capacity, alongside biological labor and elite domination.','Secondary synthesis; opposition to machine intelligence is not a total ban on minor robots, and job security is not established as the motive.'),
 ('corpus','Corpus','WARFRAME Wiki contributors','https://warframe.fandom.com/wiki/Corpus','A profit-seeking corporate hierarchy combines robotic proxies, advanced security and human crew labor.','Automated combat forces do not establish whole-population wage independence; a denied current wiki URL and forum speculation were not evidence.')
]
S=[source('src-b77-'+sid,title,author,url,'lore_reference','Bounded public or indexed lore/history passage',claim,limits) for sid,title,author,url,claim,limits in refs]
o=['src-b77-orokin']
R=[record('warframe-orokin-selective-automation-ban','c0627','Warframe — Orokin selective suppression of machine autonomy','Warframe','The Orokin empire’s technologically constrained biological labor hierarchy',['game'],
 scope('Warframe game lore','Established Orokin rule before its final collapse','Living human and human-derived subjects of the Orokin order',['Minor robots as universally banned','Clone laborers as machines rather than persons','Every Cephalon as an independently governing AI','The later Corpus as the same economy']),
 'The Orokin possess extraordinary productive technology but selectively suppress true machine intelligence while relying on biological and human-derived servants. The reference explicitly connects this choice with rejection of broader robotic automation, making it an interpretive zero variant. Minor robots still exist, so the policy is not a blanket rejection of machinery. Its evident context is elite security and domination; preserving ordinary people’s employment is not established as the motive. That limitation matters when comparing it with straightforward make-work laws.\n\nPower remains concentrated in the Orokin ruling caste, rather than spread among the workers or delegated to an autonomous machine sovereign. The guarantee estimate is weak for the scoped subjects because coercion, human trafficking and extreme punishments undermine secure access, although individual elite comfort can be high. Cloned and engineered people perform real labor and are not removed from the participation denominator because of their origins. No all-person work rate is available, so that axis remains unresolved. The later Corpus and the post-collapse world are separate economies.',
 {'guarantees':0.8,'control':0,'nonworking':None},
 {'guarantees':assessment(0.8,[0.45,1],'low','The empire’s subject population faces servitude, trafficking and severe coercive withdrawal of security; elite comfort is not general entitlement.',o),
  'control':assessment(0,[0,0.1],'medium','The human-derived Orokin elite controls subjects and constrains machine intelligence.',o),
  'nonworking':assessment(None,None,'low','Biological and human-derived servants do useful labor, but no all-person census is provided.',o)},
 0,o,[evidence('The ruling civilization selectively restricts machine intelligence despite capacity and retains biological labor.',o,'Overview: automation restrictions, biological engineering and elite subject relations','secondary_game_lore_synthesis')],
 ['Interpretive zero variant: control, not demonstrated job security, motivates the restriction.', 'Selective machine-intelligence suppression is not a ban on all robotics.', 'Biological/human-derived workers remain persons doing useful work.', 'Secondary synthesis and participation uncertainty remain explicit.'],record_type='zero_variant',analogy=[3])]
rows=[
 ('c0617','needs_evidence',['remnant'],'Remnant terraforming and angaran creation do not establish ordinary work-independent necessities.','Environmental infrastructure and species origin leave household production and access unresolved.'),
 ('c0618','needs_evidence',['forerunner'],'The ecumene’s occupational hierarchy and ancillas do not establish ordinary household post-work entitlements.','Advanced engineering and ceremonial commands cannot supply missing access rules or a participation census; no Forerunner novels are needed for this short disposition.'),
 ('c0619','needs_evidence',['created'],'Created rule promises to solve material deprivation but the checked reference does not establish implementation.','Guardian enforcement and an AI welfare program are distinct from realized durable household provision.'),
 ('c0620','needs_evidence',['ancestors'],'Ancient human technological power does not establish work-independent material allocation.','War, devolution and later stored patterns cannot fill the prewar civilian economic gap.'),
 ('c0621','needs_evidence',['ueg'],'UEG/UNSC institutions and automation do not establish a general civilian support floor.','Political authority and military employment are not proof of an enacted jobs-preservation program or automatic household entitlement.'),
 ('c0622','needs_evidence',['covenant'],'Covenant technical dependence does not establish a general post-work civilian economy.','Huragok are useful biological/artificial persons doing work; a faction reference cannot define empire-wide resource distribution.'),
 ('c0623','needs_evidence',['golden-age'],'Golden Age prosperity and Warminds do not establish an ordinary automatic necessities-allocation system.','A forum’s post-scarcity shorthand is insufficient; research and technical power do not replace the missing access rules.'),
 ('c0624','needs_evidence',['last-city'],'The Last City’s protection and science do not establish work-independent household access.','Civilian crisis work and defense remain useful activities; safety alone is not a complete material economy.'),
 ('c0625','boundary_case',['vex'],'The Vex continuously transform worlds rather than form a verified supported human post-work population.','Cyber-organic computation and captured minds do not supply a common human welfare denominator.'),
 ('c0626','boundary_case',['exo'],'Europa’s Exo research and human-derived workforce are not a verified leisure support society.','Experimental embodiment and memory maintenance preserve useful workers, without establishing a general labor-independent allocation system.'),
 ('c0628','needs_evidence',['corpus'],'Corpus robot proxies and profits do not establish whole-population material access independent of labor.','Automated security is real, while human crew and hierarchical corporations continue; neither free necessities nor deliberate unnecessary employment was verified.')
]
D=[decision(cid,status,reason,['src-b77-'+s for s in ss],analysis=analysis,follow_up='Save the short disposition and continue without reading a full lore cycle to recover the material economy.') for cid,status,ss,reason,analysis in rows]
D.append(decision('c0627','zero_variant','Selective suppression of capable machine intelligence alongside biological labor supports an explicitly interpretive zero variant.',o,society_id=R[0]['id']))
D.sort(key=lambda x:x['candidate_id'])
write_batch(77,[f'c{i:04}' for i in range(617,629)],S,R,D,[
 'Twelve ordered fast dispositions and one explicitly interpretive zero variant; no novels, ARG material or full game transcripts read.',
 'Forerunner technology and occupational-rate reference sections were enough to record the access gap; the lead was not rescued through novel reading.',
 'Orokin restrictions are selective, with control rather than demonstrated job preservation as their motive. Human-derived labor is not relabeled machine output.',
 'Destiny role-play economies, Halo counterfactual battles and forum jobs-program speculation were discarded. Empty targeted primary-search results were not treated as lore proof.',
 'An inaccessible current Warframe wiki was respected; a clearly identified indexed older wiki reference was used without pretending full-page access.'
])
